              test gate runs the headless TeslaSync.App.Tests project (the sibling-W7 convention).

=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection,
  unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.Source.cs (the generated-client feed), <Name>.ViewModel.cs
  (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view), exactly as the sibling W7
  DLQInspectorPage / SchemaDriftPage do. The generated prompt's idealized "IngestXRayPage.xaml +
  IngestXRayPageViewModel.cs under TeslaSync/Features/Admin" is mapped onto these real conventions; the surface
  registers with the W4 ShellPageFactory by route name ("IngestXRay", already in RouteTable.cs → /admin/ingest-xray).
- The page COMPOSES the four ingest-xray sub-surfaces that already exist (W3): XRayControls, XRayBucketChart,
  XRayFieldsTable (feature-views/, namespace TeslaSync.App.FeatureViews.IngestXRay) and the XRayHeader stat tiles
  (rendered through the shared XRayHeaderProjection + TsStatCard from the page's single read, namespace
  TeslaSync.App.FeatureViews). The page owns the orchestration the web page owns: the selected vehicle gates the
  X-Ray query (web useIngestXRay enabled only for a positive id); windowSel / bucketSel re-key the query.
- Data binding (ADR-004): the two manifest data sources are the web hooks useVehicles / useIngestXRay. The
  view-model reads through one injected port (IIngestXRayPageFeed, IngestXRayPage.Model.cs) with FetchVehiclesAsync
  + FetchXRayAsync; the default EmptyIngestXRayPageFeed resolves the empty state (the DLQInspectorPage/SchemaDriftPage
  host-injection precedent), and the generated-client-backed IngestXRayPageClientFeed (IngestXRayPage.Source.cs)
  binds to the generated OpenAPI contract operations get_api_v1_vehicles / get_api_v1_system_ingest_xray_vehicleID,
  asserted against the generated endpoint table + the FakeApiClient in tests. No HTTP touches the view. The X-Ray
  read fills the {vehicleID} path slot and appends snake_case window/bucket/limit query (never camelCase, never a
  double /api/v1 prefix); the JSON round-trips through the tolerant parsers (snake_case + camelCase aliases).
- The web page passes PageContainer `query={xray}`, so the body always renders the children; the X-Ray data states
  surface per ADR-006 as visible Fluent regions: loading -> the page-tier TsDataFreshness chip (IsFetching →
  "Updating…") + the XRayHeader em-dash tiles + the XRayBucketChart/XRayFieldsTable "Loading…" bodies; empty ->
  zero-sample tiles + the chart/table EmptyState bodies (and the no-vehicle panel before a vehicle is picked, and
  the empty-fleet picker hint); success -> populated tiles + the bar chart + the field table; error -> a
  TsQueryError InfoBar + Retry + the freshness chip IsError ("Error"). Never a blank region.
- SI units N/A (this admin surface bears no unit fields — vehicle ids, signal field names, sample counts,
  value-kind enums and last-seen timestamps only); counts/timestamps format through the shared NumberFormatting /
  DateTimeFormatting ports inside the composed sub-surfaces at the display boundary.
- All 5 i18n keys already exist verbatim (web key names) in Strings/{en,he,ar}/Resources.resw under the
  translation.* prefix (admin.xray.pageTitle / subtitle / panels.fields / noVehicle.title / noVehicle.message); the
  surface resolves them through the ILocalizer facade with the web English defaults as fallbacks.

